@startuml AnchorDrop_Booking_Sequence
title AnchorDrop — Booking Journey Sequence\nRequest → Compatibility → Accept → Arrival Unlock → Delay → Complete

skinparam backgroundColor #F5F1E8
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #0B1F33
  FontColor #0B1F33
}

skinparam actor {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #0B1F33
  FontColor #0B1F33
}

skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #0B1F33
  BorderColor #C6A56B
  FontColor #F5F1E8
}

skinparam lifeLineBorderColor #0B1F33
skinparam lifeLineBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #C6A56B

skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF8EE
  BorderColor #C6A56B
  FontColor #0B1F33
}

actor "Boater" as B
participant "Web Portal\n(Next.js UI)" as UI
participant "API Layer\n(Route Handlers)" as API
participant "Compatibility\nEngine" as COMP
database "MongoDB" as DB
actor "Dock Owner" as O

== Authentication & Vessel Setup ==

B -> UI : Register / Login (role = boater)
UI -> API : POST /api/auth/login
API -> DB : Find user + verify bcrypt hash
DB --> API : User document
API --> UI : Session / JWT cookie
UI --> B : Open Boater Dashboard

B -> UI : Create vessel profile\n(LOA, beam, draft, type, registration)
UI -> API : POST /api/vessels
API -> DB : Insert vessel (userId)
DB --> API : Vessel saved
API --> UI : Vessel JSON
UI --> B : Vessel listed under My Vessels

== Discovery & Compatibility ==

B -> UI : Explore docks (filters:\ncity/waterway, length, depth, price)
UI -> API : GET /api/docks?filters...
API -> DB : Query docks (public projection)
note right of API
  Public projection EXCLUDES
  arrivalInstructions
end note
DB --> API : Dock list
API --> UI : Cards / details
UI --> B : Compare listings

B -> UI : Select berth + vessel → Check fit
UI -> API : POST /api/bookings/check-compatibility
API -> COMP : Compare vessel vs dock limits
COMP --> API : { length, beam, draft, overall }
API --> UI : Compatibility result
UI --> B : Show Compatible / Not compatible

alt Vessel is NOT compatible
  B -> UI : Choose another berth or vessel
else Vessel is compatible
  == Booking Request ==
  B -> UI : Submit reservation\n(dates + special requests)
  UI -> API : POST /api/bookings
  API -> COMP : Re-validate compatibility (server-side)
  COMP --> API : Pass
  API -> DB : Insert booking status = pending
  DB --> API : Booking id
  API --> UI : Booking created
  UI --> B : Trip status = Pending

  == Owner Review ==
  O -> UI : Open Owner Dashboard → Requests
  UI -> API : GET /api/bookings/owner
  API -> DB : Find bookings for ownerId\n(+ vessel + boater details)
  DB --> API : Pending requests
  API --> UI : Request center data
  UI --> O : Show boater + vessel specs + dates

  alt Owner Rejects
    O -> UI : Reject request
    UI -> API : PATCH /api/bookings/:id/status { rejected }
    API -> DB : Update status = rejected
    DB --> API : OK
    API --> UI : Updated booking
    UI --> O : Status = Rejected
    UI --> B : Status = Rejected\n(no arrival instructions)
  else Owner Accepts
    O -> UI : Accept request
    UI -> API : PATCH /api/bookings/:id/status { accepted }
    API -> DB : Update status = accepted
    DB --> API : OK
    API --> UI : Updated booking
    UI --> O : Status = Accepted

    == Arrival Instructions Unlock ==
    B -> UI : Open trip details
    UI -> API : GET /api/bookings/boater
    API -> DB : Load booking + dock
    API -> API : If accepted → include\narrivalInstructions
    API --> UI : Booking + private arrival info
    UI --> B : Gate code · Slip · VHF channel

    == Optional Delay Reporting ==
    B -> UI : Report delay (new ETA + note)
    UI -> API : PATCH /api/bookings/:id/delay
    API -> DB : Save delayEta + delayNote
    DB --> API : OK
    API --> UI : Delay saved
    UI --> B : Delay confirmed
    UI --> O : Arrivals & Delay Alerts updated

    == Completion ==
    O -> UI : Mark booking completed\n(or system/admin flow)
    UI -> API : PATCH /api/bookings/:id/status { completed }
    API -> DB : Update status = completed
    DB --> API : OK
    API --> UI : Done
    UI --> B : Trip status = Completed
    UI --> O : Booking closed
  end
end

legend right
  |= Step |= Outcome |
  | Compatibility | Fewer unsuitable requests |
  | Pending | Shared status of truth |
  | Accepted | Unlocks private arrival data |
  | Delay | Owner sees updated ETA in-app |
  | Completed | Lifecycle closed for both sides |
  | Stack | Next.js API + MongoDB — no external booking API required |
endlegend

@enduml
